    {
      "beat_id": "B06",
      "act": "II — How it works",
      "narration_text": "Repo sensei runs four stages. It clones the repository. It parses every file into a syntax tree. It indexes what it found. And only then will it answer you.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "manim",
        "lane": "manim",
        "show": [
          {
            "at": 0.0,
            "event": "four boxes appear left to right: CLONE, PARSE, INDEX, ANSWER"
          },
          {
            "at": 0.7,
            "event": "a terracotta arrow travels through all four"
          }
        ]
      },
      "scene_label": "Pipeline",
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B06.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 9.98,
      "render_duration_s": 10.0,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B06.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-10-26T18:51:41"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B07",
      "act": "II — How it works",
      "narration_text": "The parsing is the part most tools skip. It does not grep for text. It uses tree sitter, the same parser your editor uses, so it sees a function as a function.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "manim",
        "lane": "manim",
        "show": [
          {
            "at": 0.0,
            "event": "source code lines on the left"
          },
          {
            "at": 0.5,
            "event": "a syntax tree grows node by node on the right, connected by lines"
          }
        ]
      },
      "scene_label": "TreeSitter",
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B07.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 9.28,
      "render_duration_s": 9.291666666666666,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B07.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-10-26T18:51:41"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B08",
      "act": "II — How it works",
      "narration_text": "Eighteen query files describe what to look for. Definitions. Calls. Imports. References. Across python, typescript and javascript.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "manim",
        "lane": "manim",
        "show": [
          {
            "at": 0.0,
            "event": "five labelled chips appear: defs, calls, imports, refs, strings"
          },
          {
            "at": 0.6,
            "event": "three language tags settle underneath"
          }
        ]
      },
      "scene_label": "Queries",
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B08.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 8.49,
      "render_duration_s": 8.5,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B08.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-10-26T18:51:41"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B09",
      "act": "II — How it works",
      "narration_text": "That is what makes a trace possible. One feature, followed from the button a user clicks, through the A P I that handles it, down to the table it writes.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "manim",
        "lane": "manim",
        "show": [
          {
            "at": 0.0,
            "event": "three stacked boxes: UI, API, DATABASE"
          },
          {
            "at": 0.5,
            "event": "a terracotta line connects them top to bottom and lights each in turn"
          }
        ]
      },
      "scene_label": "Trace",
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B09.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 8.51,
      "render_duration_s": 8.541666666666666,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B09.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-10-26T18:51:41"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B10",
      "act": "II — How it works",
      "narration_text": "And every answer comes back attached to the place it came from. A file. A line number. Something you can open and disagree with.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "manim",
        "lane": "manim",
        "show": [
          {
            "at": 0.0,
            "event": "an answer card on the left"
          },
          {
            "at": 0.5,
            "event": "an arrow snaps to a file chip on the right reading defs.scm colon fourteen"
          }
        ]
      },
      "scene_label": "Citation",
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B10.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 7.55,
      "render_duration_s": 7.583333333333333,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B10.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-10-26T18:51:41"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B11",
      "act": "II — How it works",
      "narration_text": "Four terms worth keeping. The index is the searchable map. A citation is the file and line. A trace follows one feature across layers. And an eval tests the answers rather than the code.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "illustrate",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeDefinitions",
          "props": {
            "title": "Four terms",
            "folderLabel": "@HumanitariansAI",
            "terms": [
              {
                "term": "Index",
                "meaning": "The searchable map of the code"
              },
              {
                "term": "Citation",
                "meaning": "The file and line an answer came from"
              },
              {
                "term": "Trace",
                "meaning": "One feature, followed across layers"
              },
              {
                "term": "Eval",
                "meaning": "A test for answers, not for code"
              }
            ]
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B11.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-26T22:02:57.792360+00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B11.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 10.75,
